## 3. Recommended Integration Workflow

1. **Client-Side Rendering (Dynamic):** If players can discover custom isotopes or dynamically alter elements in-game, run the `SpriteCanvas` generation directly in the UI component when a monster is encountered.
2. **Build-Time Generation (Asset Caching):** If you prefer static assets for faster loading, create a Node.js CLI script inside your repository (`scripts/generate-sprites.ts`) using `node-canvas`. Run it during build to populate `public/assets/sprites/` as lightweight $64\times 64$ indexed PNG files.
